Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(agent):=20daily=20plan=20budget=20is=20term?=
 =?UTF-8?q?inal=20=E2=80=94=20never=20masked=20by=20provider=20fallbacks?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The metering proxy answered a budget-exhausted chat with its correct 429
('Daily token budget reached for the plus plan…'), but the conversation
loop classified it as a generic rate limit, retried, then walked the
stock fallback chain — and the user saw the LAST dead slot's noise
('HTTP 401: Authentication Fails (governor)') instead of the budget
message. That also defeats the desktop's calm allowance card, which
matches on 'daily token budget'.

New FailoverReason.entitlement_budget: detected first in the classifier
pipeline via the proxy's unique code/message, not retryable, no
credential rotation, no fallback. The conversation loop surfaces the
proxy's message verbatim and aborts until the UTC-midnight reset.

Also: the sign-in overlay's 'updates automatically' line now swaps to a
concrete hint after 45s of waiting on the browser handoff (press Open
Nemesis in the tab / use email+password), instead of promising forever.

193/193 error-classifier tests pass (one new: budget 429 is terminal).
